Here is a practical ROS 2 troubleshooting command cheat sheet for this project.

**Build And Source**
```bash
cd ~/ros2_ws_latest
colcon build
source install/setup.bash
```

Build only these packages:
```bash
colcon build --packages-select my_robot_description my_robot_bringup
source install/setup.bash
```

**Run The Robot**
Display URDF in RViz:
```bash
ros2 launch my_robot_description display.launch.xml
```

Run Gazebo simulation:
```bash
ros2 launch my_robot_bringup my_robot_gazebo.launch.xml
```

Drive the robot with keyboard:
```bash
ros2 run teleop_twist_keyboard teleop_twist_keyboard
```

If velocity topic is different:
```bash
ros2 run teleop_twist_keyboard teleop_twist_keyboard --ros-args -r cmd_vel:=/cmd_vel
```

**Package Checks**
List packages:
```bash
ros2 pkg list
```

Find your packages:
```bash
ros2 pkg list | grep my_robot
```

Show package path:
```bash
ros2 pkg prefix my_robot_description
ros2 pkg prefix my_robot_bringup
```

List package executables:
```bash
ros2 pkg executables my_robot_description
ros2 pkg executables my_robot_bringup
```

**Nodes**
List running nodes:
```bash
ros2 node list
```

Inspect a node:
```bash
ros2 node info /robot_state_publisher
```

Common nodes to check:
```bash
ros2 node info /gazebo
ros2 node info /robot_state_publisher
```

**Topics**
List topics:
```bash
ros2 topic list
```

List topics with message types:
```bash
ros2 topic list -t
```

Inspect a topic:
```bash
ros2 topic info /cmd_vel
ros2 topic info /odom
ros2 topic info /tf
ros2 topic info /camera/image_raw
```

Echo topic data:
```bash
ros2 topic echo /odom
ros2 topic echo /cmd_vel
ros2 topic echo /camera/image_raw
ros2 topic echo /tf
```

Check publish rate:
```bash
ros2 topic hz /odom
ros2 topic hz /tf
ros2 topic hz /camera/image_raw
```

Publish velocity manually:
```bash
ros2 topic pub /cmd_vel geometry_msgs/msg/Twist "{linear: {x: 0.2}, angular: {z: 0.0}}"
```

Turn in place:
```bash
ros2 topic pub /cmd_vel geometry_msgs/msg/Twist "{linear: {x: 0.0}, angular: {z: 0.5}}"
```

Stop robot:
```bash
ros2 topic pub --once /cmd_vel geometry_msgs/msg/Twist "{linear: {x: 0.0}, angular: {z: 0.0}}"
```

**Services**
List services:
```bash
ros2 service list
```

List services with types:
```bash
ros2 service list -t
```

Show service type:
```bash
ros2 service type /spawn_entity
```

Call empty service:
```bash
ros2 service call /reset_simulation std_srvs/srv/Empty
ros2 service call /reset_world std_srvs/srv/Empty
```

Pause/unpause Gazebo:
```bash
ros2 service call /pause_physics std_srvs/srv/Empty
ros2 service call /unpause_physics std_srvs/srv/Empty
```

**TF And Frames**
Show TF tree:
```bash
ros2 run tf2_tools view_frames
```

Echo transform:
```bash
ros2 run tf2_ros tf2_echo odom base_footprint
ros2 run tf2_ros tf2_echo base_link camera_link
ros2 run tf2_ros tf2_echo camera_link camera_link_optical
```

Check robot state:
```bash
ros2 topic echo /robot_description
ros2 topic echo /joint_states
```

**URDF/Xacro Checks**
Expand xacro:
```bash
xacro src/my_robot_description/urdf/my_robot.urdf.xacro
```

Save expanded URDF:
```bash
xacro src/my_robot_description/urdf/my_robot.urdf.xacro > /tmp/my_robot.urdf
```

Check URDF:
```bash
check_urdf /tmp/my_robot.urdf
```

**Gazebo Checks**
See spawned model/entity:
```bash
ros2 topic list | grep gazebo
ros2 service list | grep gazebo
```

If robot does not move, check:
```bash
ros2 topic info /cmd_vel
ros2 topic echo /cmd_vel
ros2 topic echo /odom
ros2 node list
```

**Camera Checks**
List image topics:
```bash
ros2 topic list | grep camera
ros2 topic list | grep image
```

Echo camera info:
```bash
ros2 topic echo /camera/camera_info
```

View image:
```bash
ros2 run rqt_image_view rqt_image_view
```

**Useful GUI Tools**
```bash
rqt
rqt_graph
rviz2
```

For this project, your main launch command is:

```bash
ros2 launch my_robot_bringup my_robot_gazebo.launch.xml
```

Then in another terminal:

```bash
ros2 topic pub /cmd_vel geometry_msgs/msg/Twist "{linear: {x: 0.2}, angular: {z: 0.0}}"
```
